# Horizon

Horizon is an event-sourced engineering memory. Phase 1 stores harness knowledge only: rules, skills, prompts, and evaluations. Decisions, pull requests, review findings, incidents, and a knowledge-graph product are out of scope. If a task needs one of them, stop and ask. Do not scaffold them.

## Stack

Use Supabase for every capability it already provides: Postgres, Auth, RLS, Storage, Realtime, and queues, cron, or pgvector only when a feature needs them.

Custom command logic and every AI workflow live in Kotlin with Koog (`services/agent`). Do not put that logic in Edge Functions or in the web app.

GitHub App webhooks are delivered to `services/agent`. The service verifies `X-Hub-Signature-256`, dedupes `X-GitHub-Delivery`, and appends to `events`. Do not point GitHub at an Edge Function, at `apps/web`, or at Supabase. Phase 1 does not ingest GitHub events. The path is specified in `idea.md`.

## Layout

- `supabase/` — config, migrations, seed
- `services/agent/` — Kotlin, Ktor, Koog
- `apps/web/` — Vite, React, TypeScript

## Authority

An AI result is a proposal. A human organization member approves it. The agent service account must not append `ProposalApproved` or directly change a rule, skill, prompt, or evaluation.

A verification verdict comes from a schema check, a lint, a hook, or a test. A model must not judge compliance. `ProposalVerified` records that mechanical result, or `NotConfigured` when no such check exists.

Jev is a `ProposalVerifier` port in `services/agent`. The phase-1 implementation returns `NotConfigured`. Do not call the TypeSafe API in this phase.

## Language

Identifiers, schema names, comments, commits, and rules are English.

## Tenancy

Every tenant-owned row has `org_id`. RLS checks organization membership. Never authorize from `user_metadata`. Local seed is one organization; the schema stays multi-tenant.
